        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Pakistan Vehicle Tax Guide: Token Tax, Transfer Fees, and Calculator</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: July 2026 | 9 min read</p>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <p>Owning a vehicle in Pakistan means navigating provincial token tax rates, withholding taxes, registration fees, and transfer charges. Each province — Sindh, Punjab, KPK, and Islamabad — administers its own vehicle tax through its Excise and Taxation Department. Rates depend on engine capacity, vehicle age, vehicle type, and whether you are an FBR tax filer or non-filer.</p>

            <p>This Pakistan vehicle tax guide explains token tax rates across major provinces, transfer fees, how your filer status affects your bill, and how to pay online. You can also use our <a href="/countries/pakistan/vehicle/vehicle-tax-calculator">vehicle tax calculator Pakistan</a> to compare rates instantly.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Understanding Vehicle Token Tax</h2>
            <p>Vehicle token tax is an annual fee that certifies your vehicle for legal road use. It is distinct from the federal advance tax deducted at the time of vehicle purchase and is collected by provincial authorities. The tax year runs from <strong>1 July to 30 June</strong>. If you pay your full annual token tax before <strong>31 August</strong>, most provinces grant a <strong>10% early-payment rebate</strong>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Sindh Vehicle Tax</h2>
            <p>Sindh manages vehicle tax through the excise.gos.pk portal and the e-Payment GOS app. Key features of Sindh vehicle tax include:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>New cars up to 1000cc:</strong> One-time lifetime token tax of PKR 20,000, eliminating annual payments for the vehicle's life.</li>
              <li><strong>Motorcycles up to 149cc:</strong> Very low annual rates (as low as PKR 80 per year).</li>
              <li><strong>Online payment:</strong> Generate a PSID through the e-Payment GOS app and pay via banking app, ATM, or mobile wallet.</li>
              <li><strong>Smart card fee:</strong> New registrations in Sindh incur an additional PKR 750 smart card fee.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Sindh's digital infrastructure makes online payments straightforward, but you must verify the PSID number before paying to avoid misapplied payments.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Islamabad Vehicle Token Tax</h2>
            <p>Islamabad follows a CC-based token tax structure under the Federal Withholding Tax schedule. Rates are among the most progressive in Pakistan:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Up to 850cc:</strong> PKR 10,000 for filers, PKR 20,000 for non-filers</li>
              <li><strong>1300–1499cc:</strong> PKR 2,500 for filers, PKR 5,000 for non-filers</li>
              <li><strong>Larger engines:</strong> Progressive bands up to PKR 20,000+ for high-capacity vehicles</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Islamabad also exempts vehicles 10 years or older from withholding tax, though a reduced base token tax still applies. This exemption provides relief to owners of older cars who keep their vehicles running longer.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Punjab Vehicle Tax</h2>
            <p>Punjab has adopted a hybrid system where locally manufactured cars are taxed by engine capacity, while imported vehicles may be taxed by invoice value. Key points include:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Engine capacity brackets:</strong> Rates start from PKR 800 per year for small vehicles and go up to PKR 18,000+ for larger cars and SUVs.</li>
              <li><strong>Lifetime token tax:</strong> Cars up to 1000cc can opt for a one-time PKR 20,000 lifetime payment in Punjab.</li>
              <li><strong>Commercial vehicles:</strong> Typically charged 1.5x private rates. SUVs and 4x4s may attract an additional 20% surcharge.</li>
              <li><strong>ePay Punjab:</strong> Online payment through the ePay Punjab app or website using a 17-digit PSID.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">KPK Vehicle Tax</h2>
            <p>Khyber Pakhtunkhwa applies vehicle tax under Section 234 of the Income Tax Ordinance. The filer advantage is pronounced:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>1600–1999cc:</strong> PKR 6,000 for filers versus PKR 12,000 for non-filers</li>
              <li><strong>2000cc+:</strong> PKR 12,000 for filers versus PKR 24,000 for non-filers</li>
              <li><strong>Motorcycles:</strong> One-time lifetime token tax of PKR 1,000</li>
              <li><strong>Online payment:</strong> Partially available through KPK Excise portals</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Vehicle Transfer Fees</h2>
            <p>When buying or selling a vehicle, you must pay transfer fees to update ownership records. Transfer fees vary by province but typically include:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>New registration fee:</strong> 1% to 5% of vehicle value, depending on engine size and province</li>
              <li><strong>Transfer fee:</strong> Ranges from PKR 200 to PKR 4,000 depending on vehicle class</li>
              <li><strong>Smart card or data card fee:</strong> Around PKR 1,300 per issuance</li>
              <li><strong>Penalty for late registration:</strong> Escalating fines if the vehicle is not registered within 30 days of purchase</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The seller must clear all outstanding token tax before the transfer proceeds. Both parties need CNIC copies and the original registration book.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How to Calculate Vehicle Tax</h2>
            <p>Your total vehicle tax bill includes base token tax, withholding tax, transfer fees, and any applicable surcharges. To get an accurate estimate, our <a href="/countries/pakistan/vehicle/vehicle-tax-calculator">vehicle tax calculator Pakistan</a> allows you to:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li>Select your province (Punjab, Sindh, KPK, Islamabad, or Balochistan)</li>
              <li>Enter vehicle type, engine capacity, and age</li>
              <li>Choose filer or non-filer status</li>
              <li>Instantly see base token tax, advance tax, transfer fees, and total payable</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Vehicle taxation in Pakistan varies by province, but one truth holds everywhere: filers pay significantly less than non-filers. Maintaining your FBR Active Taxpayer List status can cut your vehicle token tax bill in half in some provinces. Use our <a href="/countries/pakistan/vehicle/vehicle-tax-calculator">vehicle tax calculator Pakistan</a> to compare rates across provinces and plan your next purchase or transfer with confidence.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the vehicle token tax rate in Sindh?</h3>
            <p>Sindh offers a one-time lifetime token tax of PKR 20,000 for new cars up to 1000cc. Motorcycles up to 149cc pay just PKR 80 annually. Payment is made online through excise.gos.pk or the e-Payment GOS app.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How do I pay vehicle token tax online in Islamabad?</h3>
            <p>Use the MTMIS Islamabad portal or FBR online channels. Enter your vehicle registration number to view your token tax, generate a PSID, and pay via banking or mobile channels.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Do filers pay less vehicle tax than non-filers?</h3>
            <p>Yes. In many provinces, filers pay exactly half the non-filer rate on withholding tax. A 1800cc car in KPK costs PKR 6,000 per year for filers but PKR 12,000 for non-filers.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the 10% token tax rebate?</h3>
            <p>Several provinces, including Punjab, offer a 10% discount if you pay the full annual token tax on or before 31 August. For example, a PKR 4,500 token becomes PKR 4,050 with the rebate.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Are vehicles over 10 years old exempt from token tax?</h3>
            <p>Vehicles older than 10 years are exempt from withholding tax in most provinces under the Income Tax Ordinance, but they still pay a portion of the base token tax (typically around 75%).</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What are the vehicle transfer fees in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>Transfer fees range from PKR 200 to PKR 4,000 depending on vehicle class and province. New registration fees are 1% to 5% of invoice value. Smart card fees may add another PKR 1,300.</p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is lifetime token tax?</h3>
            <p>Lifetime token tax is a one-time payment option available in Punjab and Sindh for small vehicles. Once paid, you are exempt from annual token tax for that vehicle for its lifetime. In Punjab, cars up to 1000cc pay PKR 20,000 once.</p>
